# B011: 512-row Block Krylov calibration against exact SVD and matched power

Development hypothesis: stabilized Block Krylov provides a viable strong refresh endpoint for the real Landmark prefix and, at equal matrix passes, its enlarged Krylov space should not be worse than simultaneous power. This tests a classical baseline; it is not a new method.

Data: first512 rows of the pinned71952x2704 Landmark matrix, no scaling, k=25. Convert only those rows to float64 dense. Independent exact thin SVD supplies optimum Frobenius/spectral residuals and the reference right subspace. Preserve source hashes and matrix-slice hash.

Arms: Gaussian seeds101,102,103; block width35 (k plus10); q in[0,1,2,4,7]. For every seed/q run stabilized Block Krylov and simultaneous power from the identical Gaussian matrix. Reorthogonalize after each A.T and A multiply; Block Krylov concatenates all powered blocks and performs a final QR. Both compute the right factors from the SVD of Q.T@A. Matrix pass count is2q+2, including initial A Omega and final Q.T A; QR and small SVD time remain included in full method time. Record state array bytes, not just passes. The exact SVD is a quality/control baseline; one timing is calibration evidence, not a speed claim.

Metrics computed independently: Frobenius residual ratio to exact optimum; spectral residual ratio from the largest eigenvalue of `AA.T-(A@V.T)(A@V.T).T`; projection distance `sqrt(2k-2||V V_exact.T||_F^2)`; maximum per-vector captured-energy error normalized by sigma_26^2. Clip only tiny negative roundoff in Gram eigenvalues and record magnitude.

Predictions and predeclared decisions:

1. At every matched seed/q, Block Krylov Frobenius and spectral ratios should be no worse than power by more than1e-10 in exact arithmetic; an observed excess over1e-8 triggers implementation/numerical audit.
2. Endpoint readiness requires all three seeds at one common q<=7 to achieve Frobenius ratio<=1+1e-8 and spectral ratio<=1+1e-6. Projection equality is reported but is not a readiness gate because near-degenerate leading spaces can differ while task quality is preserved.
3. If ready, choose the smallest common q prospectively from these thresholds and next test the71-refresh eta=.1 trajectory with repeated isolated timing against exact refresh. If no q is ready, retain the negative result and do not integrate it online or tune beyond q7 without a changed mechanism hypothesis.

All15 pairs and failures are retained. This is one correlated real prefix and three algorithm seeds, not independent dataset confirmation or nominal probability validation. CPU one thread through `cpu_guard.py`,4GiB address-space cap, timeout300s. Expected peak below750MiB from prior Landmark records and current2.69GB shared headroom; abort on memory error and do not fall back silently.
